al Boma-Bungu secteur. No armed group holds territory in the area, which lies far from the eastern conflict zones. Moanda town, Banana and the villages are policed by the PNC, while the large Kitona base (FARDC training centre and air base) and its associated camps are military-run, with a Force Navale presence at Banana. Security issues are crime, oil-sector related tensions and occasional Bundu dia Kongo-related political unrest, none of which displaced state control. Web research was unavailable in this run (search budget exhausted), so the assessment rests on default state presence."}}